{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/particulate-nature/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/particulate-nature.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Particulate Nature of Matter | Chemistry Foundations","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Foundations\n      </a>\n      <!-- Progress indicator -->\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-sky-400 to-blue-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -atom text-sky-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"atom\">atom</span>Particulate Nature of Matter\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding that matter consists of tiny particles in constant motion - the foundation of chemistry.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-sky-50 border-l-4 border-sky-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-sky-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-sky-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• State the kinetic theory of matter</li>\n          <li>• Describe the arrangement and motion of particles in solids, liquids, and gases</li>\n          <li>• Explain changes of state using particle theory</li>\n          <li>• Describe evidence for the particulate nature of matter</li>\n          <li>• Define diffusion and explain it using kinetic theory</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: What is Matter Made Of? -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-sky-100 text-sky-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What is Matter Made Of?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The <strong class=\"text-sky-600\">Kinetic Theory of Matter</strong> states that all matter is made up of tiny particles (atoms, molecules, or ions) that are in constant, random motion.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-sky-100 to-blue-100 p-4 rounded-lg text-center mb-4\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-800 font-medium\">Key Principle:</p>\n            <p class=\"text-xl font-bold text-sky-700\">All matter consists of particles in constant motion</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Important Note</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Particles are too small to be seen directly. We know they exist from indirect evidence like diffusion, Brownian motion, and changes of state.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: States of Matter -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-sky-100 text-sky-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          States of Matter\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Matter exists in three main states: <strong>solid</strong>, <strong>liquid</strong>, and <strong>gas</strong>. The state depends on how the particles are arranged and how they move.</p>\n          \n          <!-- Visual comparison -->\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <!-- Solid -->\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-center\">\n              <div class=\"mb-3\">\n                <svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 80\" class=\"w-full h-20 mx-auto\">\n                  <!-- Solid particles - closely packed, regular arrangement -->\n                  <circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"20\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"35\" cy=\"20\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"20\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"20\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"20\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"40\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"35\" cy=\"40\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"40\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"40\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"40\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"35\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#ef4444\"></circle>\n                </svg>\n              </div>\n              <h4 class=\"font-bold text-red-700 mb-2\">SOLID</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-xs text-gray-600 text-left space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Closely packed</li>\n                <li>• Regular pattern</li>\n                <li>• Vibrate in place</li>\n                <li>• Fixed shape &amp; volume</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            \n            <!-- Liquid -->\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-center\">\n              <div class=\"mb-3\">\n                <svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 80\" class=\"w-full h-20 mx-auto\">\n                  <!-- Liquid particles - close but random -->\n                  <circle cx=\"15\" cy=\"35\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"28\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"45\" cy=\"32\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"62\" cy=\"25\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"78\" cy=\"30\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"22\" cy=\"50\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"48\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"55\" cy=\"42\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"72\" cy=\"48\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"85\" cy=\"45\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"30\" cy=\"62\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"58\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"68\" cy=\"65\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"></circle>\n                </svg>\n              </div>\n              <h4 class=\"font-bold text-blue-700 mb-2\">LIQUID</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-xs text-gray-600 text-left space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Close together</li>\n                <li>• Random arrangement</li>\n                <li>• Move around each other</li>\n                <li>• Fixed volume, takes shape of container</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            \n            <!-- Gas -->\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-center\">\n              <div class=\"mb-3\">\n                <svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 80\" class=\"w-full h-20 mx-auto\">\n                  <!-- Gas particles - far apart, random -->\n                  <circle cx=\"10\" cy=\"15\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"35\" cy=\"8\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"20\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"12\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"15\" cy=\"45\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"45\" cy=\"55\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"40\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"25\" cy=\"70\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n                  <circle cx=\"85\" cy=\"65\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#22c55e\"></circle>\n                </svg>\n              </div>\n              <h4 class=\"font-bold text-green-700 mb-2\">GAS</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-xs text-gray-600 text-left space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Far apart</li>\n                <li>• Random arrangement</li>\n                <li>• Move fast in all directions</li>\n                <li>• No fixed shape or volume</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Comparison Table -->\n        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-gray-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <thead class=\"bg-sky-600 text-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-left\">Property</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Solid</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Liquid</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Gas</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody class=\"bg-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Particle arrangement</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Close, regular</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Close, random</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Far apart, random</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Particle motion</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Vibrate only</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Slide past each other</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Move rapidly in all directions</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Shape</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Fixed</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Takes container shape</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Fills container</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Volume</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Fixed</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Fixed</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Variable</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Compressibility</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Incompressible</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Slightly compressible</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Easily compressible</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Energy of particles</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Low</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Medium</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">High</td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Changes of State -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-sky-100 text-sky-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Changes of State\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">When matter is heated or cooled, particles gain or lose energy. This causes changes of state.</p>\n          \n          <!-- State Change Diagram -->\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n              <div class=\"bg-red-100 px-6 py-4 rounded-lg text-center min-w-[100px]\">\n                <p class=\"font-bold text-red-700 text-lg\">SOLID</p>\n              </div>\n              \n              <div class=\"flex flex-col items-center\">\n                <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">melting</span>\n                <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-2xl text-green-500 md:rotate-0 rotate-90\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">freezing</span>\n                <span class=\"mi -arrow-left text-2xl text-blue-500 md:rotate-0 rotate-90\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>\n              </div>\n              \n              <div class=\"bg-blue-100 px-6 py-4 rounded-lg text-center min-w-[100px]\">\n                <p class=\"font-bold text-blue-700 text-lg\">LIQUID</p>\n              </div>\n              \n              <div class=\"flex flex-col items-center\">\n                <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">evaporating</span>\n                <span class=\"mi -arrow-right text-2xl text-green-500 md:rotate-0 rotate-90\" data-mi=\"arrow_forward\">arrow_forward</span>\n                <span class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">condensing</span>\n                <span class=\"mi -arrow-left text-2xl text-blue-500 md:rotate-0 rotate-90\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>\n              </div>\n              \n              <div class=\"bg-green-100 px-6 py-4 rounded-lg text-center min-w-[100px]\">\n                <p class=\"font-bold text-green-700 text-lg\">GAS</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-up mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_upward\">arrow_upward</span>Melting &amp; Evaporation</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-red-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Particles gain energy</li>\n                <li>• Move faster and further apart</li>\n                <li>• Overcome forces of attraction</li>\n                <li>• Temperature stays constant during change</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-down mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_downward\">arrow_downward</span>Freezing &amp; Condensation</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Particles lose energy</li>\n                <li>• Move slower and closer together</li>\n                <li>• Forces of attraction increase</li>\n                <li>• Temperature stays constant during change</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Sublimation -->\n        <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -exchange-alt mr-2\" data-mi=\"swap_horiz\">swap_horiz</span>Sublimation</h4>\n          <p class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm mb-2\">Some substances change directly from solid to gas without becoming liquid. This is called <strong>sublimation</strong>.</p>\n          <p class=\"text-purple-600 text-sm\"><strong>Examples:</strong> Dry ice (solid CO₂), iodine, naphthalene (mothballs)</p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Evidence for Particles -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-sky-100 text-sky-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Evidence for Particles\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <!-- Diffusion -->\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -wind text-sky-500 mr-2\" data-mi=\"air\">air</span>Diffusion\n            </h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\"><strong class=\"text-sky-600\">Diffusion</strong> is the movement of particles from a region of higher concentration to a region of lower concentration.</p>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded-lg mb-3\">\n              <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Examples of diffusion:</strong></p>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1 mt-2\">\n                <li>• A drop of ink spreading in water</li>\n                <li>• The smell of perfume spreading through a room</li>\n                <li>• Tea bag color spreading in hot water</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-3 rounded-r-lg\">\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\"><strong>Key point:</strong> Diffusion is faster in gases than liquids because gas particles have more energy and move faster. It's slowest in solids.</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <!-- Brownian Motion -->\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-5 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -random text-purple-500 mr-2\" data-mi=\"shuffle\">shuffle</span>Brownian Motion\n            </h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\"><strong class=\"text-purple-600\">Brownian motion</strong> is the random, zigzag movement of tiny particles suspended in a fluid. It was first observed by Robert Brown in 1827.</p>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n              <p class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm\"><strong>Explanation:</strong> The visible particles (like pollen) are being hit by invisible, fast-moving water molecules. The uneven bombardment causes the random motion.</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Worked Examples -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-sky-100 text-sky-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Worked Examples\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <!-- Example 1 -->\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-sky-50 text-left font-semibold text-sky-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-sky-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -question-circle mr-2 text-sky-500\" data-mi=\"help\">help</span>Why does diffusion happen faster in gases than liquids?</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-sky-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Answer:</strong></p>\n                    <p class=\"text-sky-700 mt-1\">Gas particles have <strong>more kinetic energy</strong> and move <strong>much faster</strong> than liquid particles. They are also <strong>farther apart</strong> with weaker forces between them, allowing faster movement from high to low concentration.</p>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <!-- Example 2 -->\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-green-50 text-left font-semibold text-green-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-green-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -question-circle mr-2 text-green-500\" data-mi=\"help\">help</span>Why does temperature stay constant during melting?</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Answer:</strong></p>\n                    <p class=\"text-green-700 mt-1\">All the heat energy supplied is used to <strong>break the bonds</strong> between particles (overcome forces of attraction) rather than increase kinetic energy. The temperature only rises once all the solid has melted.</p>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <!-- Example 3 -->\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -question-circle mr-2 text-purple-500\" data-mi=\"help\">help</span>Explain why gases are easily compressed but solids are not.</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Answer:</strong></p>\n                    <p class=\"text-purple-700 mt-1\">In gases, particles are <strong>far apart</strong> with large empty spaces between them. These spaces can be reduced by compression. In solids, particles are <strong>closely packed</strong> with little space between them, so they cannot be compressed further.</p>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-sky-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Describe the arrangement and motion of particles in a solid.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p><strong>Arrangement:</strong> Particles are closely packed in a regular, fixed pattern.</p>\n                <p><strong>Motion:</strong> Particles can only vibrate about their fixed positions. They cannot move from place to place.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Name the process: gas → liquid</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p><strong>Condensation</strong> - particles lose energy, move slower, and come closer together.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Why does a gas fill any container it is placed in?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Gas particles have high kinetic energy and move rapidly in all directions. There are weak forces between particles, so they spread out to fill all the available space.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. What is Brownian motion and what does it prove?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Brownian motion is the random, zigzag movement of particles suspended in a fluid. It proves that matter consists of tiny particles in constant motion, because the visible particles are being bombarded by invisible molecules.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-7\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-sky-50 to-blue-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-sky-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-sky-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways for WAEC/JAMB/NECO</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-sky-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• All matter consists of tiny particles in constant motion</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Solid:</strong> close packed, vibrate only, fixed shape &amp; volume</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Liquid:</strong> close but random, slide past each other, fixed volume</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Gas:</strong> far apart, move rapidly, no fixed shape or volume</li>\n            <li>• Diffusion proves particles exist and move</li>\n            <li>• Temperature stays constant during state changes</li>\n            <li>• Gases diffuse fastest; solids slowest</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  <!-- Topic Tracking and Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-sky-50 to-blue-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card {\n      transition: all 0.2s ease;\n    }\n    .step-card:hover {\n      transform: translateX(4px);\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn {\n      transition: all 0.3s ease;\n    }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover {\n      transform: scale(1.02);\n    }\n    .particle-animation {\n      position: relative;\n      height: 120px;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #e0f2fe, #bae6fd);\n      border-radius: 8px;\n    }\n    .particle {\n      position: absolute;\n      width: 10px;\n      height: 10px;\n      background: #3b82f6;\n      border-radius: 50%;\n      animation: move 2s infinite alternate;\n    }\n    @keyframes move {\n      0% { transform: translate(0, 0); }\n      100% { transform: translate(20px, 10px); }\n    }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":{"topicId":"particulate-nature","topicTitle":"Particulate Nature of Matter","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}